---
import Presentation from "../../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const PII = `PERSONALLY IDENTIFIABLE INFORMATION (PII)

  information about an individual that identifies,
  links, relates, or describes them

  Social Security number      medical information
  age                         financial information
  race                        biometric data
  phone number(s)

Four verbs. "Describes them" is much wider
than "names them."`;

const Collected = `WHAT GETS RECORDED WITHOUT YOU DOING ANYTHING

  search engines      a history of your searches
  websites            a history of who viewed them
  devices, websites
  and networks        your location

  programs            where you have been, how you
                      got there, and how long you
                      stayed`;

const Aggregation = `THE IDEA THAT MATTERS MOST

  "Disparate personal data, such as geolocation,
   cookies, and browsing history, can be AGGREGATED
   to create knowledge about an individual."

No single item identifies you.
Put them together and they do.`;

const Benefit = `AND IT IS NOT ALL COST

  PII and other information placed online can be
  used to ENHANCE a user's online experiences.

  PII stored online can SIMPLIFY making online
  purchases.

Both of those are in the framework.
The trade is real in both directions.`;

const Unintended = `USED IN WAYS THAT WERE NOT INTENDED

  an email message may be forwarded
  tweets can be retweeted
  social media posts can be viewed by
    potential employers

And: "Once information is placed online,
it is difficult to delete."`;

const Deduce = `THE ONE THAT ENDS THE SESSION

  "Information posted to social media services can
   be used by others. Combining information posted
   on social media AND OTHER SOURCES can be used to
   DEDUCE PRIVATE INFORMATION ABOUT YOU."

Not information you posted.
Information you did not post, worked out from
information you did.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Activity 3.16: PII, Aggregation, and Privacy</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Brief -->
        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Last Three Sessions</h2>

          <p>
            <b>Everything so far in this block has been about effects on people in
            general.</b> The last three are about effects on <i>you</i> &mdash; your
            data, your accounts, and the people who want them.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">And the central idea today is one you have already
            met, at session 43.</b> You stripped the location out of a photo's metadata
            and the image did not change. Today is what happens when nobody strips it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Activity 3.16</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">PII, Aggregation, and Privacy</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Concepts</h2>
              <p>What Counts as PII</p>
              <p>Aggregation</p>
              <p>Difficult to Delete</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>The Definition</h2>
              <Code code={PII} frame="code" lang="txt" title="PII" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">Identifies, <b>links</b>, <b>relates</b>, or <b>describes</b>.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Wider Than You Think</h2>
              <p><b>Age is on the list. Race is on the list.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">Neither identifies anyone on its own.</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                They are PII because they <b>describe</b> a person &mdash; and because
                of what happens when you combine them.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Collected Without You Acting</h2>
              <Code code={Collected} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Just By Existing Online" showLineNumbers={false} />
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Read That Last One Again</h2>
              <p><b>Where you have been. How you got there. How long you stayed.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">That is not a location. <b>That is a pattern of life.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">And no single record of it is remarkable.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Which Is the Whole Point</h2>
              <Code code={Aggregation} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Aggregation" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">
                <b class="text-sn-theme">Harmless plus harmless plus harmless can equal
                identified.</b>
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>You Have Seen This Shape</h2>
              <p>Session 43: metadata on a photo. Date, device, location.</p>
              <p class="fragment">Each one boring. Together: <b>where you were, when, and with what.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">This is that, at the scale of everything you do.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>It Buys You Things</h2>
              <Code code={Benefit} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Both Directions" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">Saved addresses. Recommendations that are right. One-tap payment.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>And It Has a Price List</h2>
              <p>Search history can be used <b>to suggest websites</b>&hellip;</p>
              <p class="fragment">&hellip;or <b>for targeted marketing</b>.</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Same data. Same mechanism. <b>Session 70's single effect, viewed two
                ways.</b>
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Curation Can Be Exploited</h2>
              <p>
                <b>&quot;Commercial and governmental curation of information may be
                exploited if privacy and other protections are ignored.&quot;</b>
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">The data was gathered for one reason. It is available for others.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>It Escapes</h2>
              <Code code={Unintended} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Beyond What You Meant" showLineNumbers={false} />
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>And It Can Be Used Against You</h2>
              <p>
                <b>PII can be used to stalk or steal the identity of a person</b>, or to
                aid in planning other criminal acts.
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">That sentence is in the framework, in those words.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>The Sentence That Ends the Session</h2>
              <Code code={Deduce} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Deduce" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p class="fragment">You control what you post. <b>You do not control what it implies.</b></p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>One Thing You Can Do</h2>
              <p>
                <b>&quot;Users can control the permissions programs have for collecting
                user information. Users should review the permission settings of
                programs to protect their privacy.&quot;</b>
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">The framework's one piece of practical advice on this topic.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today's Objectives</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Defining PII and recognizing what counts</li>
                <li>Describing what is collected without any deliberate action</li>
                <li>Explaining aggregation, and why harmless data stops being harmless</li>
                <li>Describing both the benefits and the risks of PII online</li>
                <li>Explaining why information online is difficult to delete</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Key Terms</h2>
              <div class="text-start">
                <dl>
                  <dt>PII</dt>
                  <dd>Personally identifiable information &mdash; information that identifies, links, relates to, or describes an individual.</dd>
                  <dt>Aggregation</dt>
                  <dd>Combining disparate data to create knowledge about an individual that no single item provided.</dd>
                  <dt>Curation</dt>
                  <dd>The gathering and organizing of information by a commercial or governmental body.</dd>
                </dl>
              </div>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Today's Work</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 1: Is It PII?</h3>

          <p>
            <b>The definition is: identifies, links, relates to, or describes an
            individual.</b> Yes or no, and which of the four verbs applies.
          </p>

          <ol>
            <li>A Social Security number</li>
            <li>Your age</li>
            <li>The model of phone you own</li>
            <li>A fingerprint</li>
            <li>The town you live in</li>
            <li>A list of every website you visited last Tuesday</li>
            <li>Your favorite color</li>
          </ol>

          <p>
            <b>Items 3, 5 and 7 are the arguable ones.</b> For each, describe what
            would have to be combined with it to make it identify somebody.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 2: Build a Person From Nothing</h3>

          <p>
            <b>Four pieces of data. None of them names anybody.</b>
          </p>

          <table class="table table-sm align-middle mt-3">
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><b>1</b></td><td>A phone was at a particular school between 8am and 3pm on weekdays</td></tr>
              <tr><td><b>2</b></td><td>The same phone is at one address every night</td></tr>
              <tr><td><b>3</b></td><td>It searched for &quot;driving test near me&quot; three times last month</td></tr>
              <tr><td><b>4</b></td><td>It was at a hospital on a Tuesday afternoon</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <ol>
            <li><b>What do you know about this person</b> after item 1 alone? After 1 and 2 together?</li>
            <li>What does item 3 add?</li>
            <li>
              <b>Could you narrow this to a single individual?</b> Say what else you
              would need.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Item 4 is different from the other three.</b> Say how, and why that
              matters more than the rest.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Which single item, removed, would help most?</b> Defend your choice.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">This is aggregation, and none of the four items is
            PII on its own.</b>
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 3: The Trade, Honestly</h3>

          <p>For each, name <b>what you get</b> and <b>what you give</b>.</p>

          <table class="table table-sm align-middle mt-3">
            <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>What you get</th><th>What you give</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>A shop saving your address and card</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td>A map app suggesting your usual route home</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td>A music app building a weekly recommendation list</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td>A fitness band recording your heart rate all day</td><td></td><td></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <ol>
            <li><b>Which of the four would you accept?</b> There is no right answer.</li>
            <li><b>Which would you refuse, and what exactly are you refusing?</b></li>
            <li>
              For the one you would refuse: <b>is the risk the data itself, or what it
              could be combined with?</b>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Task 4: Difficult to Delete</h3>

          <p>
            <b>A student posts something they regret. They delete it an hour later.</b>
          </p>

          <ol>
            <li><b>Name three places it could still exist.</b></li>
            <li>Why does &quot;I deleted it&quot; not mean &quot;it is gone&quot;?</li>
            <li>
              The framework says information can be used in ways that were not
              intended, and gives three examples. <b>Name all three.</b>
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Now the harder one.</b> Somebody works out something private about this
              student that the student never posted, by combining what they did post
              with something else. <b>Give a plausible example.</b>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Give the four verbs in the definition of PII.</li>
            <li>Name three things collected about you without any deliberate action.</li>
            <li>What is aggregation, and why does it matter?</li>
            <li>Name one benefit of PII being stored online.</li>
            <li>What can users do about permissions?</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer these before submitting your work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>At session 43 you deleted the location from a photo's metadata and the image was unchanged. Explain what that activity was really demonstrating, now that you have met aggregation.</li>
            <li>&quot;Age&quot; is listed as PII and age alone identifies nobody. Explain why it is on the list anyway.</li>
            <li>Name one permission on a device you use. Say what it enables and what it costs, and whether you would turn it off.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>All four tasks, plus your reflection.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Activity Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
